{"source_id": "W2129021195", "title": "Note-taking and review: The role of note-taking method and review in learning", "year": 2017, "abstract": "The present study examined the effects of note-taking method (longhand vs. laptop) and review (review vs. no review) on learning. Participants viewed a lecture and took notes either longhand or on a laptop, then either reviewed their notes or did not, and completed a test of recall. Results showed no significant main effect of note-taking method and no significant interaction between note-taking method and review; however, there was a significant main effect of review, such that participants who reviewed their notes outperformed those who did not."}
